#: slug-sync.php:2295
msgid "Recommended"
msgstr ""

#: slug-sync.php:2296
msgid "Best for most sites and large stores. Changes only the URL slug, keeps the existing modified date, and avoids triggering save automations, webhooks, or integration syncs for every item. Redirect protections and reports are still created."
msgstr ""

#: slug-sync.php:2302
#: slug-sync.php:2879
msgid "Standard WordPress update"
msgstr ""

#: slug-sync.php:2303
msgid "Saves every item through WordPress normally. This updates its modified date and runs plugins, webhooks, and automations connected to saving. Choose this only when another integration must react to each slug change; it can be much slower."
msgstr ""

#: slug-sync.php:2310
msgid "What is included"
msgstr ""

#: slug-sync.php:2311
msgid "By default, only published items whose slug clearly differs from the title are included. Leave these unchecked unless you need the broader scope described."
msgstr ""

#: slug-sync.php:2316
msgid "Also include unpublished items"
msgstr ""

#: slug-sync.php:2317
msgid "Includes drafts, pending-review items, and private items. Leave off if you only want to change URLs that visitors can currently access."
msgstr ""

#: slug-sync.php:2323
msgid "Recheck numbered slugs"
msgstr ""

#: slug-sync.php:2324
msgid "Includes slugs that already match the title except for a number. These are skipped by default because the number often marks a duplicate title. WordPress may add a number again when it is needed to keep the URL unique."
msgstr ""

